<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-BOS Intl sets A$50 mln fungible bond-Westpac.</title>
<headline>RTRS-BOS Intl sets A$50 mln fungible bond-Westpac.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>BOS International (Australia) has issued a A$50 million bond, fungible with its outstanding A$100 million 6.5 percent November 15, 2001 bond, lead manager Westpac Banking Corporation said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The bond was priced at 31 basis points over the 12.0 percent November 2001 bond and carries a rating of A-plus by Standard &amp; Poor's.</p>
<p>Bank of Scotland is the guarantor.</p>
<p>The issue is made under BOS International's A$1.0 billion combined commercial paper and medium term note programme.</p>
<p>--Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
